  "designBoundaries": [
    "The existing controller owns linear movement/friction and recovery. Cosmetic randomness never feeds gameplay velocity or replay randomness.",
    "The posed contact lever and surface-tangent travel drive angular friction; floor-normal twist damps separately. Rotation is bounded to 16 radians/second.",
    "The ground-hit notification records input eligibility only. Actual contact impulses own hard-hit motion; nearly settled contacts do not add a generic flail. Player attempts still work.",
    "The grounded solve allocates no buffers or vectors. It samples the same twelve posed joint spheres from existing world matrices, with no extra world or mesh query."
  ],
